IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`

-- sga-part2.l4: Part 2 (sections 6 to 12A) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth),
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- Every defined term of section 6(1) is in sga-defs.l4 (the term, how the text defines it, what it points at, the text as printed).
-- This module holds the rules the definitions and the interpretation sections create; the counting of days lives in sga-time.l4.
-- A term the text defines by pointing at another Act or instrument is not given a meaning here: the fact is a plain input.

§ `Section 6(1): definitions that are worked out from facts`

-- src:94 | arrangement, for the purposes of section 30, means:
-- src:95 | (a) an agreement, arrangement, understanding, promise or undertaking, whether express or implied, and whether or not enforceable, or intended to be enforceable, by legal proceedings; or
-- src:96 | (b) any scheme, plan, proposal, action, course of action or course of conduct.
@ref s 6(1) "arrangement" (src:94-96)
GIVEN `is an agreement, arrangement, understanding, promise or undertaking, express or implied, enforceable or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a scheme, plan, proposal, action, course of action or course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an arrangement for the purposes of section 30` MEANS
        `is an agreement, arrangement, understanding, promise or undertaking, express or implied, enforceable or not`
    OR `is a scheme, plan, proposal, action, course of action or course of conduct`

-- src:143 | government body means:
-- src:144 | (a) the Commonwealth or a State or Territory; or
-- src:145 | (b) a Commonwealth, State or Territory authority.
@ref s 6(1) "government body" (src:143-145)
GIVEN `is the Commonwealth or a State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a Commonwealth, State or Territory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a government body` MEANS
    `is the Commonwealth or a State or Territory` OR `is a Commonwealth, State or Territory authority`

-- src:168 | part-time employee means a person who is employed to work not more than 30 hours per week.
@ref s 6(1) "part-time employee" (src:168-168)
GIVEN `hours per week the person is employed to work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a part-time employee` MEANS
    `hours per week the person is employed to work` AT MOST 30

-- "ordinary time earnings": (a) and (b), other than a termination lump sum of a kind in (c) or (d).
-- src:162 | ordinary time earnings, for a person, means all of the person’s earnings as an employee made up of:
-- src:163 | (a) earnings in respect of ordinary hours of work; and
-- src:164 | (b) earnings consisting of over-award payments, shift-loading or commission;
-- src:165 | other than a lump sum payment of any of the following kinds made to the person on the termination of the person’s employment:
-- src:166 | (c) a payment in lieu of unused sick leave;
-- src:167 | (d) an unused annual leave payment, or unused long service leave payment, within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997.
@ref s 6(1) "ordinary time earnings" (src:162-167)
GIVEN `earnings in respect of ordinary hours of work` IS A NUMBER
      `earnings consisting of over-award payments, shift-loading or commission` IS A NUMBER
      `lump sum payments on termination in lieu of unused sick leave, or unused annual leave or long service leave payments, included in those earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ordinary time earnings of a person` MEANS
    (`earnings in respect of ordinary hours of work` PLUS `earnings consisting of over-award payments, shift-loading or commission`)
    MINUS `lump sum payments on termination in lieu of unused sick leave, or unused annual leave or long service leave payments, included in those earnings`

-- src:199 | superannuation provider means:
-- src:200 | (a) the trustee of a complying superannuation fund; or
-- src:201 | (b) the trustee of a complying approved deposit fund; or
-- src:202 | (c) an RSA provider.
@ref s 6(1) "superannuation provider" (src:199-202)
GIVEN `is the trustee of a complying superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the trustee of a complying approved deposit fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an RSA provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a superannuation provider` MEANS
    `is the trustee of a complying superannuation fund` OR `is the trustee of a complying approved deposit fund` OR `is an RSA provider`

-- src:203 | superannuation scheme means:
-- src:204 | (a) a defined benefit superannuation scheme whether or not embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund; or
-- src:205 | (b) any other scheme embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund.
@ref s 6(1) "superannuation scheme" (src:203-205)
GIVEN `is a defined benefit superannuation scheme, whether or not embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is any other scheme embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a superannuation scheme` MEANS
    `is a defined benefit superannuation scheme, whether or not embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund`
    OR `is any other scheme embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund`

-- src:177 | public sector scheme means a scheme of superannuation established:
-- src:178 | (a) by or under a law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory; or
-- src:179 | (b) under the authority of:
-- src:180 | (i) the Commonwealth or the government of a State or Territory; or
-- src:181 | (ii) a municipal corporation, another local governing body or a public authority constituted by or under a law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory.
@ref s 6(1) "public sector scheme" (src:177-181)
GIVEN `established by or under a law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `established under the authority of the Commonwealth or the government of a State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `established under the authority of a municipal corporation, another local governing body or a public authority constituted by or under such a law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a public sector scheme` MEANS
        `established by or under a law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory`
    OR `established under the authority of the Commonwealth or the government of a State or Territory`
    OR `established under the authority of a municipal corporation, another local governing body or a public authority constituted by or under such a law`

-- src:228 | unfunded public sector scheme means a public sector scheme that is a defined benefit superannuation scheme:
-- src:229 | (a) in respect of which no fund is established for the purposes of the scheme; or
-- src:230 | (b) under which all or some of the amounts that will be required for the payment of benefits are not paid into the fund established for the purposes of the scheme or are not paid until the members become entitled to receive the benefits.
@ref s 6(1) "unfunded public sector scheme" (src:228-230)
GIVEN `is a public sector scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a defined benefit superannuation scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no fund is established for the purposes of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some or all amounts required to pay benefits are not paid into the fund, or not until the members become entitled to the benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an unfunded public sector scheme` MEANS
        `is a public sector scheme`
    AND `is a defined benefit superannuation scheme`
    AND (`no fund is established for the purposes of the scheme`
         OR `some or all amounts required to pay benefits are not paid into the fund, or not until the members become entitled to the benefits`)

DECLARE `Trustee of a scheme` IS ONE OF
    `the trustee of the fund`
    `the person who manages the scheme`

-- src:209 | trustee, in relation to a superannuation scheme, means:
-- src:210 | (a) if:
-- src:211 | (i) the scheme is embodied in the governing rules of a fund; and
-- src:212 | (ii) there is a trustee of the fund;
-- src:213 | the trustee of the fund; or
-- src:214 | (b) in any other case—the person who manages the scheme.
-- src:215 | trustee, except in relation to a superannuation fund or superannuation scheme, includes:
-- src:216 | (a) a person appointed or constituted trustee by:
-- src:217 | (i) act of parties; or
-- src:218 | (ii) order or declaration of a court; or
-- src:219 | (iii) operation of law; and
-- src:220 | (b) an executor, administrator or other personal representative of a deceased person; and
-- src:221 | (c) a guardian or committee; and
-- src:222 | (d) a receiver or receiver and manager; and
-- src:223 | (e) a liquidator of a company; and
-- src:224 | (f) a person:
-- src:225 | (i) having or taking upon himself or herself the administration or control of any real or personal property affected by any express or implied trust; or
-- src:226 | (ii) acting in any fiduciary capacity; or
-- src:227 | (iii) having the possession, control or management of any real or personal property of a person under any legal or other disability.
@ref s 6(1) "trustee" (in relation to a superannuation scheme) (src:209-227)
GIVEN `the scheme is embodied in the governing rules of a fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a trustee of the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Trustee of a scheme`
`the trustee in relation to a superannuation scheme` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is embodied in the governing rules of a fund` AND `there is a trustee of the fund`
    THEN `the trustee of the fund`
    ELSE `the person who manages the scheme`

-- "defined benefit member", subject to section 6AA: the regulations may prescribe circumstances in which a member is not, or is taken to be, one.
-- src:126 | defined benefit member, subject to section 6AA, means a member entitled on retirement to be paid a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to either or both of the following:
-- src:127 | (a) the amount of the member’s salary:
-- src:128 | (i) at the date of the member’s retirement or an earlier date; or
-- src:129 | (ii) averaged over a period before retirement;
-- src:130 | (b) a specified amount.
@ref s 6(1) "defined benefit member", s 6AA (src:126-130)
-- src:238 | 6AA Interpretation: defined benefit member
-- src:239 | The regulations may prescribe:
-- src:240 | (a) circumstances in which a member of a superannuation fund is not a defined benefit member for the purposes of this Act, or a provision of this Act; and
-- src:241 | (b) circumstances in which a member of a superannuation fund who is not otherwise a defined benefit member is to be taken to be a defined benefit member for the purposes of this Act, or a provision of this Act.
@ref s 6(1) "defined benefit member", s 6AA (src:238-241)
GIVEN `is entitled on retirement to a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to the salary of the member at retirement or an earlier date, or averaged over a period before retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is entitled on retirement to a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to a specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations prescribe that the member is not a defined benefit member in these circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations prescribe that the member is to be taken to be a defined benefit member in these circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a defined benefit member` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the regulations prescribe that the member is not a defined benefit member in these circumstances` AND `the regulations prescribe that the member is to be taken to be a defined benefit member in these circumstances` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the regulations prescribe that the member is not a defined benefit member in these circumstances` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the regulations prescribe that the member is to be taken to be a defined benefit member in these circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST (`by salary` OR `by a specified amount`)
    WHERE
        `by salary` MEANS `is entitled on retirement to a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to the salary of the member at retirement or an earlier date, or averaged over a period before retirement`
        `by a specified amount` MEANS `is entitled on retirement to a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to a specified amount`

-- src:237 | (2) For the purposes of this Act, a reference to a contribution made by an employer for the benefit of an employee includes a reference to a contribution made on behalf of the employer.
@ref s 6(2) (src:237-237)
GIVEN `the contribution is made by the employer for the benefit of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contribution is made on behalf of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a contribution made by an employer for the benefit of an employee` MEANS
    `the contribution is made by the employer for the benefit of the employee` OR `the contribution is made on behalf of the employer`

§ `Sections 6A and 6B: defined benefit schemes and conversion notices`

-- src:243 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), a defined benefit superannuation scheme is a scheme under which:
-- src:244 | (a) one or more members of the scheme are entitled, on retirement, to be paid a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to either or both of the following:
-- src:245 | (i) the amount of the member’s annual salary:
-- src:246 | (A) at the date of the member’s retirement; or
-- src:247 | (B) at a date before retirement; or
-- src:248 | (C) averaged over a period of employment before retirement;
-- src:249 | (ii) a specified amount; and
-- src:250 | (b) if the scheme is not a public sector scheme—some or all of the contributions under the scheme (out of which, together with earnings on those contributions, the benefits are to be paid) are not paid into a fund, or accumulated in a fund, in respect of any individual member but are paid into and accumulated in a fund in the form of an aggregate amount.
@ref s 6A(1), (2) (src:243-250)
-- src:251 | (2) A scheme embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund (other than a scheme of the kind referred to in subsection (1)) is a defined benefit superannuation scheme if a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund or scheme.
@ref s 6A(1), (2) (src:251-251)
GIVEN `a member is entitled on retirement to a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to annual salary at retirement, at an earlier date or averaged over a period of employment before retirement, or to a specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme is a public sector scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some or all contributions are paid into and accumulated in a fund in the form of an aggregate amount, not in respect of any individual member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme is embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund or scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a defined benefit superannuation scheme` MEANS
        (    `a member is entitled on retirement to a benefit defined, wholly or in part, by reference to annual salary at retirement, at an earlier date or averaged over a period of employment before retirement, or to a specified amount`
         AND (`the scheme is a public sector scheme` OR `some or all contributions are paid into and accumulated in a fund in the form of an aggregate amount, not in respect of any individual member`))
    OR (`the scheme is embodied in the governing rules of a superannuation fund` AND `a conversion notice has effect in relation to the fund or scheme`)

-- src:252 | (3) If the conversion notice is expressed to take effect on a day before the day on which the notice is given, the scheme in question is taken to have been a defined benefit superannuation scheme from the day on which the notice is expressed to take effect.
@ref s 6A(3) (src:252-252)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice is expressed to take effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day a scheme is taken to have been a defined benefit superannuation scheme from` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice is expressed to take effect` LESS THAN `the day the notice is given`
    THEN JUST `the day the notice is expressed to take effect`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:253 | (4) Subsection (3) has effect regardless of the making of any assessment, or the payment of any superannuation guarantee charge, in respect of a QE day after the conversion notice took effect.
@ref s 6A(4) (src:253-253)
GIVEN `an assessment has been made, or superannuation guarantee charge paid, for a QE day after the conversion notice took effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsection 6A(3) has effect` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:255 | (1) A conversion notice is a written notice by the trustee of a superannuation fund given to the Commissioner stating that the fund, or a particular superannuation scheme embodied in the governing rules of the fund, is to be treated as a defined benefit superannuation scheme for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 6B(1) (src:255-255)
GIVEN `the notice is written` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is by the trustee of a superannuation fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the fund, or a particular scheme embodied in its governing rules, is to be treated as a defined benefit superannuation scheme for the purposes of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a conversion notice` MEANS
        `the notice is written`
    AND `the notice is by the trustee of a superannuation fund`
    AND `the notice is given to the Commissioner`
    AND `the notice states that the fund, or a particular scheme embodied in its governing rules, is to be treated as a defined benefit superannuation scheme for the purposes of the Act`

-- 6B(4): not effective unless, before it is given, the trustee gives written notice of the intention and the proposed date of effect to each employer contributing for the benefit of defined benefit members.
-- src:263 | (4) A conversion notice or a revocation notice will not be effective unless, before it is given, the trustee gives written notice of:
-- src:264 | (a) the trustee’s intention to give the notice; and
-- src:265 | (b) the proposed date of effect of the notice;
-- src:266 | to each employer contributing to the fund or scheme for the benefit of employees as defined benefit members of the fund or scheme.
@ref s 6B(4) (src:263-266)
GIVEN `the trustee gave written notice of its intention to give the notice to each employer contributing for the benefit of employees as defined benefit members, before giving it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee gave written notice of the proposed date of effect to each such employer, before giving it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a conversion notice or revocation notice is effective` MEANS
        `the trustee gave written notice of its intention to give the notice to each employer contributing for the benefit of employees as defined benefit members, before giving it`
    AND `the trustee gave written notice of the proposed date of effect to each such employer, before giving it`

-- 6B(2): a conversion notice that is effective takes effect on the day specified in it.
-- src:256 | (2) Subject to subsection (4), a conversion notice takes effect in relation to the fund or scheme on the day specified in the notice. Subject to subsection (4), the trustee may, by written notice (revocation notice) given to the Commissioner, revoke the conversion notice.
@ref s 6B(2) (src:256-256)
GIVEN `the notice is effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day specified in the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day a conversion notice takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the notice is effective` THEN JUST `the day specified in the notice` ELSE NOTHING

-- 6B(3): the earliest day a notice may be expressed to take effect is in sga-time.l4; a stated day earlier than that is not covered by the text.
-- src:257 | (3) A conversion notice may be expressed to take effect on a day that is not earlier than:
-- src:258 | (a) if the notice is given before 15 May in a quarter starting on 1 April—1 January in the previous quarter; or
-- src:259 | (b) if the notice is given before 15 August in a quarter starting on 1 July—1 April in the previous quarter; or
-- src:260 | (c) if the notice is given before 15 November in a quarter starting on 1 October—1 July in the previous quarter; or
-- src:261 | (d) if the notice is given before 15 February in a quarter starting on 1 January—1 October in the previous quarter; or
-- src:262 | (e) in any other case—the first day of the quarter in which the notice is given.
@ref s 6B(3) (src:257-262)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice is expressed to take effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a conversion notice may be expressed to take effect on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice is expressed to take effect` AT LEAST `the earliest day a conversion notice may be expressed to take effect` `the day the notice is given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:267 | (5) If, while the conversion notice is in effect, an employer begins contributing to the fund or scheme for the benefit of employees as defined benefit members of the fund or scheme, the trustee must give the employer written notice of:
-- src:268 | (a) the giving of the conversion notice; and
-- src:269 | (b) the date of effect of the notice;
-- src:270 | within 7 business days of the receipt by the trustee of the employer’s first contribution.
@ref s 6B(5) (src:267-270)
GIVEN `the conversion notice is in effect when the employer begins contributing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the trustee gave the employer the written notice` IS A DATE
      `the day the trustee received the first contribution of the employer` IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the trustee gave the employer notice of the conversion notice in time` MEANS
    IF `the conversion notice is in effect when the employer begins contributing`
    THEN `an act is within n business days of an event` `the day the trustee gave the employer the written notice` `the day the trustee received the first contribution of the employer` 7 holidays
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 7, 7A and 8: borrowed meanings`

-- src:271 | 7 Interpretation: complying superannuation fund or scheme
-- src:272 | A superannuation fund or scheme is a complying superannuation fund or complying superannuation scheme (as the case may be) in relation to a period for the purposes of this Act if it is a complying superannuation fund in relation to that period for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997.
@ref s 7 (src:271-272)
GIVEN `it is a complying superannuation fund in relation to that period for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a complying superannuation fund or scheme in relation to a period` MEANS
    IF `it is a complying superannuation fund in relation to that period for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:273 | 7A Interpretation: complying approved deposit fund
-- src:274 | An approved deposit fund is a complying approved deposit fund at a particular time for the purposes of this Act if it is a complying approved deposit fund in relation to the year of income in which that time occurred for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997.
@ref s 7A (src:273-274)
GIVEN `it is a complying approved deposit fund in relation to the year of income in which that time occurred for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a complying approved deposit fund at a particular time` MEANS
    IF `it is a complying approved deposit fund in relation to the year of income in which that time occurred for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:275 | 8 Interpretation: resident of Australia
-- src:276 | A person is a resident of Australia for the purposes of this Act at any time when the person is a resident of Australia for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936.
@ref s 8 (src:275-276)
GIVEN `the person is a resident of Australia at that time for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a resident of Australia at a time` MEANS
    IF `the person is a resident of Australia at that time for the purposes of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 10: benefit certificates`

-- src:278 | (1) A benefit certificate is a certificate by an actuary relating to one or more specified defined benefit superannuation schemes and specifying the rate, expressed as a percentage, that is, in the opinion of the actuary, the notional employer contribution rate, in relation to a specified class of employees (being defined benefit members of the scheme or schemes, as the case may be), of an employer who is a contributor under the scheme or schemes (as the case may be) for the benefit of an employee in that class.
@ref s 10(1) (src:278-278)
GIVEN `is a certificate by an actuary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `relates to one or more specified defined benefit superannuation schemes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `specifies the rate, expressed as a percentage, that is in the opinion of the actuary the notional employer contribution rate for a specified class of employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a benefit certificate` MEANS
        `is a certificate by an actuary`
    AND `relates to one or more specified defined benefit superannuation schemes`
    AND `specifies the rate, expressed as a percentage, that is in the opinion of the actuary the notional employer contribution rate for a specified class of employees`

-- 10(3): effect runs from the date specified until the earliest of (a) to (d). NOTHING in an event's day means the event has not happened.
-- src:280 | (3) A benefit certificate has effect from the date specified in the certificate until:
-- src:281 | (a) a superannuation scheme to which it relates is amended in a way that affects, or may affect, the level or method of calculation of the minimum benefits provided under the scheme for the class of employees specified in the certificate; or
-- src:282 | (b) another benefit certificate is issued in relation to the same class of employees and the same scheme or schemes; or
-- src:283 | (c) a period of 5 years from the date of issue expires; or
-- src:284 | (d) in the case of a certificate that relates to a scheme that is a defined benefit superannuation scheme because of the operation of subsection 6A(2)—the conversion notice under section 6B is revoked;
-- src:285 | whichever occurs first.
@ref s 10(3) (src:280-285)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earlier of two events that may not have happened` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF x AT MOST y THEN JUST x ELSE JUST y

-- src:280 | (3) A benefit certificate has effect from the date specified in the certificate until:
-- src:281 | (a) a superannuation scheme to which it relates is amended in a way that affects, or may affect, the level or method of calculation of the minimum benefits provided under the scheme for the class of employees specified in the certificate; or
-- src:282 | (b) another benefit certificate is issued in relation to the same class of employees and the same scheme or schemes; or
-- src:283 | (c) a period of 5 years from the date of issue expires; or
-- src:284 | (d) in the case of a certificate that relates to a scheme that is a defined benefit superannuation scheme because of the operation of subsection 6A(2)—the conversion notice under section 6B is revoked;
-- src:285 | whichever occurs first.
@ref s 10(3) (src:280-285)
GIVEN reading IS A Counting
      `the day specified in the certificate` IS A DATE
      `the day the certificate was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the scheme was amended in a way that affects the minimum benefits` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day another certificate was issued for the same class and scheme` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the conversion notice was revoked` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a benefit certificate has effect on a day under one reading` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN `the day specified in the certificate`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the last day of n years from an event` reading `the day the certificate was issued` 5
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST expiry THEN
             CONSIDER `the earlier of two events that may not have happened`
                         (`the earlier of two events that may not have happened` `the day the scheme was amended in a way that affects the minimum benefits` `the day another certificate was issued for the same class and scheme`)
                         (`the earlier of two events that may not have happened` `the day the conversion notice was revoked` (JUST expiry))
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST end THEN
                 BRANCH IF day LESS THAN end THEN JUST TRUE
                        IF day EQUALS end THEN NOTHING
                        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:280 | (3) A benefit certificate has effect from the date specified in the certificate until:
-- src:281 | (a) a superannuation scheme to which it relates is amended in a way that affects, or may affect, the level or method of calculation of the minimum benefits provided under the scheme for the class of employees specified in the certificate; or
-- src:282 | (b) another benefit certificate is issued in relation to the same class of employees and the same scheme or schemes; or
-- src:283 | (c) a period of 5 years from the date of issue expires; or
-- src:284 | (d) in the case of a certificate that relates to a scheme that is a defined benefit superannuation scheme because of the operation of subsection 6A(2)—the conversion notice under section 6B is revoked;
-- src:285 | whichever occurs first.
@ref s 10(3) (src:280-285)
GIVEN `the day specified in the certificate` IS A DATE
      `the day the certificate was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the scheme was amended in a way that affects the minimum benefits` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day another certificate was issued for the same class and scheme` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the conversion notice was revoked` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a benefit certificate has effect on a day` MEANS
    `the two readings agree`
        (`a benefit certificate has effect on a day under one reading` `the day of the event is not counted` `the day specified in the certificate` `the day the certificate was issued` `the day the scheme was amended in a way that affects the minimum benefits` `the day another certificate was issued for the same class and scheme` `the day the conversion notice was revoked` day)
        (`a benefit certificate has effect on a day under one reading` `the day of the event is counted as the first day` `the day specified in the certificate` `the day the certificate was issued` `the day the scheme was amended in a way that affects the minimum benefits` `the day another certificate was issued for the same class and scheme` `the day the conversion notice was revoked` day)

§ `Section 10A: qualifying earnings`

DECLARE `Amounts of a person for section 10A` HAS
    `ordinary time earnings` IS A NUMBER
    `commissions payable to the person` IS A NUMBER
    `payments as a member of the executive body of a body corporate` IS A NUMBER
    `payments under a contract referred to in subsection 12(3) in respect of the labour of the person` IS A NUMBER
    `remuneration as a member of a Parliament or Legislative Assembly` IS A NUMBER
    `payments for work referred to in subsection 12(8)` IS A NUMBER
    `remuneration in circumstances referred to in subsection 12(9) or (10)` IS A NUMBER
    `reductions agreed in return for a contribution to a complying superannuation fund or an RSA, of amounts not excluded by subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
    `amount counted again because it is covered by more than one paragraph` IS A NUMBER
    `payments that represent the reversal of all or part of a sacrificed contribution` IS A NUMBER
    `amounts excluded because the regulations prescribe the employee, the work or the kind of payment` IS A NUMBER

-- With daydate imported, a chain of eight PLUS terms did not finish type-checking (each PLUS may be a day plus a number), so sums are built from two-term helpers.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum of two amounts` MEANS a PLUS b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the difference of two amounts` MEANS a MINUS b

-- src:301 | (1) A person’s qualifying earnings are amounts covered by one or more of the following paragraphs:
-- src:302 | (a) the person’s ordinary time earnings;
-- src:303 | (b) all commissions payable to the person;
-- src:304 | (c) all payments for the performance of the person’s duties as a member of the executive body (whether described as the board of directors or otherwise) of a body corporate;
-- src:305 | (d) all payments under a contract referred to in subsection 12(3) that are in respect of the person’s labour under the contract;
-- src:306 | (e) all remuneration of the person as a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth or a State or the Legislative Assembly of a Territory;
-- src:307 | (f) all payments to the person for work referred to in subsection 12(8);
-- src:308 | (g) all remuneration of the person in circumstances referred to in subsection 12(9) or (10);
-- src:309 | (h) if under an arrangement the person agreed for:
-- src:310 | (i) a contribution to be made to a complying superannuation fund or an RSA for the benefit of the person by the person’s employer; and
-- src:311 | (ii) in return, for the reduction (including to nil) of one or more amounts of a kind described in paragraphs (a) to (g) of this subsection but not in subsection (3) of this section;
-- src:312 | an amount equal to the total of those reductions.
-- src:313 | Note: For paragraph (h), reductions are not counted if they are of amounts excluded by subsection (3) from being qualifying earnings.
@ref s 10A(1), (2), (3) (src:301-313)
-- src:314 | (2) To the extent that an amount is covered by more than one paragraph of subsection (1), the amount is counted only once.
-- src:315 | Exclusions
@ref s 10A(1), (2), (3) (src:314-315)
-- src:316 | (3) However, a person’s qualifying earnings do not include any of the following:
-- src:317 | (a) a payment of an amount that represents the reversal of all or part of a sacrificed contribution;
-- src:318 | (b) earnings or remuneration of, or payments to, the person to the extent that:
-- src:319 | (i) the person is an employee of a kind prescribed by the regulations; or
-- src:320 | (ii) the earnings, remuneration or payments are for work done of a kind prescribed by the regulations; or
-- src:321 | (iii) the earnings, remuneration or payments are otherwise of a kind prescribed by the regulations.
-- src:322 | Meaning of payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee
@ref s 10A(1), (2), (3) (src:316-322)
GIVEN amounts IS A `Amounts of a person for section 10A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the qualifying earnings of a person` MEANS
    `the difference of two amounts` (`the difference of two amounts` gross again) (`the sum of two amounts` reversal excluded)
    WHERE
        gross MEANS `the sum of two amounts` (`the sum of two amounts` (`the sum of two amounts` o c) (`the sum of two amounts` x p)) (`the sum of two amounts` (`the sum of two amounts` f g) h)
        o MEANS amounts's `ordinary time earnings`
        c MEANS amounts's `commissions payable to the person`
        x MEANS `the sum of two amounts` (amounts's `payments as a member of the executive body of a body corporate`) (amounts's `payments under a contract referred to in subsection 12(3) in respect of the labour of the person`)
        p MEANS amounts's `remuneration as a member of a Parliament or Legislative Assembly`
        f MEANS amounts's `payments for work referred to in subsection 12(8)`
        g MEANS amounts's `remuneration in circumstances referred to in subsection 12(9) or (10)`
        h MEANS amounts's `reductions agreed in return for a contribution to a complying superannuation fund or an RSA, of amounts not excluded by subsection (3)`
        again MEANS amounts's `amount counted again because it is covered by more than one paragraph`
        reversal MEANS amounts's `payments that represent the reversal of all or part of a sacrificed contribution`
        excluded MEANS amounts's `amounts excluded because the regulations prescribe the employee, the work or the kind of payment`

-- src:323 | (4) A payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee by an employer means:
-- src:324 | (a) a payment of qualifying earnings to the employee by or on behalf of the employer; or
-- src:325 | (b) for qualifying earnings described by paragraph (1)(h)—the reductions described in that paragraph made in return for the making of the sacrificed contribution for the benefit of the employee.
-- src:326 | Meaning of maximum contributions base
@ref s 10A(4) (src:323-326)
GIVEN `a payment of qualifying earnings to the employee by or on behalf of the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `reductions made in return for the making of the sacrificed contribution for the benefit of the employee, for qualifying earnings described by paragraph (1)(h)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of a payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee` MEANS
    `a payment of qualifying earnings to the employee by or on behalf of the employer`
    PLUS `reductions made in return for the making of the sacrificed contribution for the benefit of the employee, for qualifying earnings described by paragraph (1)(h)`

-- 10A(5): concessional contributions cap x (100 / charge percentage), rounded down to the nearest multiple of $10 (the formula is from the formulas file of the text bundle).
-- src:327 | (5) The maximum contributions base, for a payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee, is the following amount (rounded down to the nearest multiple of $10):
-- src:328 | where:
@ref s 10A(5) (src:327-328)
-- src:327 | (5) The maximum contributions base, for a payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee, is the following amount (rounded down to the nearest multiple of $10):
@ref s 10A(5) (src:327-327)
GIVEN `the concessional contributions cap` IS A NUMBER
      `the charge percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum contributions base` MEANS
    (FLOOR (((`the concessional contributions cap` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY `the charge percentage`) DIVIDED BY 10)) TIMES 10

-- 10A(6): a payment that causes the total for the financial year to exceed the base counts only up to the base; a payment after that counts as nil.
-- src:331 | (6) For the purposes of this Act (other than this section), if an employer’s payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee during a financial year results in the employee’s total qualifying earnings:
-- src:332 | (a) during the financial year; and
-- src:333 | (b) in relation to the employer;
-- src:334 | exceeding the maximum contributions base, then treat the amount of that payment as if it were equal to:
-- src:335 | (c) if that payment caused that total to exceed that base—so much of that payment as does not include the excess; or
-- src:336 | (d) if an earlier payment had already caused that total to exceed that base—nil.
@ref s 10A(6) (src:331-336)
GIVEN `the total qualifying earnings of the employee from the employer during the financial year before the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the base for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the payment that is treated as qualifying earnings` MEANS
    BRANCH IF before AT LEAST base THEN 0
           IF (before PLUS paid) GREATER THAN base THEN base MINUS before
           OTHERWISE paid
    WHERE
        before MEANS `the total qualifying earnings of the employee from the employer during the financial year before the payment`
        paid MEANS `the payment`
        base MEANS `the base for the year`

§ `Section 12: employee and employer`

DECLARE `Engagement` HAS
    `is an employee in the ordinary meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is entitled to payment for duties as a member of the executive body of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works under a contract wholly or principally for the labour of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth or of a State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a member of the Legislative Assembly of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is paid to perform or present, or to provide services in connection with, an entertainment, sport or similar activity, or in connection with a film, tape, disc or broadcast` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds or performs the duties of an appointment, office or position under the Constitution or a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, or is otherwise in the service of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds office as a member of a local government council` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is covered by paragraph 12-45(1)(e) in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is paid to do work wholly or principally of a domestic or private nature for not more than 30 hours per week` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:338 | (1) Subject to this section, in this Act, employee and employer have their ordinary meaning. However, for the purposes of this Act, subsections (2) to (11):
-- src:339 | (a) expand the meaning of those terms; and
-- src:340 | (b) make particular provision to avoid doubt as to the status of certain persons.
@ref s 12 (src:338-340)
-- src:341 | (2) A person who is entitled to payment for the performance of duties as a member of the executive body (whether described as the board of directors or otherwise) of a body corporate is, in relation to those duties, an employee of the body corporate.
@ref s 12 (src:341-341)
-- src:342 | (3) If a person works under a contract that is wholly or principally for the labour of the person, the person is an employee of the other party to the contract.
@ref s 12 (src:342-342)
-- src:343 | (4) A member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth is an employee of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 12 (src:343-343)
-- src:344 | (5) A member of the Parliament of a State is an employee of the State.
@ref s 12 (src:344-344)
-- src:345 | (6) A member of the Legislative Assembly for the Australian Capital Territory is an employee of the Australian Capital Territory.
@ref s 12 (src:345-345)
-- src:346 | (7) A member of the Legislative Assembly of the Northern Territory is an employee of the Northern Territory.
@ref s 12 (src:346-346)
-- src:347 | (8) The following are employees for the purposes of this Act:
-- src:348 | (a) a person who is paid to perform or present, or to participate in the performance or presentation of, any music, play, dance, entertainment, sport, display or promotional activity or any similar activity involving the exercise of intellectual, artistic, musical, physical or other personal skills is an employee of the person liable to make the payment;
-- src:349 | (b) a person who is paid to provide services in connection with an activity referred to in paragraph (a) is an employee of the person liable to make the payment;
-- src:350 | (c) a person who is paid to perform services in, or in connection with, the making of any film, tape or disc or of any television or radio broadcast is an employee of the person liable to make the payment.
@ref s 12 (src:347-350)
-- src:351 | (9) A person who:
-- src:352 | (a) holds, or performs the duties of, an appointment, office or position under the Constitution or under a law of the Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; or
-- src:353 | (b) is otherwise in the service of the Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory (including service as a member of the Defence Force or as a member of a police force);
-- src:354 | is an employee of the Commonwealth, the State or the Territory, as the case requires. However, this rule does not apply to a person in the capacity of the holder of an office as a member of a local government council.
@ref s 12 (src:351-354)
-- src:355 | (9A) Subject to subsection (10), a person who holds office as a member of a local government council is not an employee of the council.
@ref s 12 (src:355-355)
-- src:356 | (10) A person covered by paragraph 12-45(1)(e) in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953 (about members of local governing bodies subject to PAYG withholding) is an employee of the body mentioned in that paragraph.
@ref s 12 (src:356-356)
-- src:357 | (11) A person who is paid to do work wholly or principally of a domestic or private nature for not more than 30 hours per week is not regarded as an employee in relation to that work.
@ref s 12 (src:357-357)
GIVEN e IS AN `Engagement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is an employee for the purposes of the Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `domestic` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `payg` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `council` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `deemed` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `domestic` MEANS e's `is paid to do work wholly or principally of a domestic or private nature for not more than 30 hours per week`
        `payg` MEANS e's `is covered by paragraph 12-45(1)(e) in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953`
        `council` MEANS e's `holds office as a member of a local government council`
        `deemed` MEANS `a deeming limb applies` OR e's `is an employee in the ordinary meaning`
        `a deeming limb applies` MEANS `limbs 2 to 4` OR `limbs 5 to 7`
        `limbs 2 to 4` MEANS e's `is entitled to payment for duties as a member of the executive body of a body corporate` OR e's `works under a contract wholly or principally for the labour of the person` OR e's `is a member of the Parliament of the Commonwealth or of a State`
        `limbs 5 to 7` MEANS e's `is a member of the Legislative Assembly of the Australian Capital Territory or of the Northern Territory` OR e's `is paid to perform or present, or to provide services in connection with, an entertainment, sport or similar activity, or in connection with a film, tape, disc or broadcast` OR e's `holds or performs the duties of an appointment, office or position under the Constitution or a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, or is otherwise in the service of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`

§ `Section 12A: references to industrial instruments`

-- src:359 | (1) In this Act, the following expressions have the same meanings as in the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009:
-- src:360 | (a) AWA;
-- src:361 | (b) collective agreement;
-- src:362 | (c) ITEA;
-- src:363 | (d) notional agreement preserving State awards;
-- src:364 | (e) old IR agreement;
-- src:365 | (f) pre-reform AWA;
-- src:366 | (g) pre-reform certified agreement;
-- src:367 | (h) preserved State agreement;
-- src:368 | (i) Division 2B State instrument;
-- src:369 | (j) State reference transitional award or common rule.
-- src:370 | Note: For an instrument referred to in this subsection, see item 4 of Schedule 2 to the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009.
@ref s 12A (src:359-370)
-- src:371 | (2) In this Act, enterprise agreement has the same meaning as in the Fair Work Act 2009.
@ref s 12A (src:371-371)
-- src:372 | (3) In this Act, workplace determination means a workplace determination made under the Fair Work Act 2009 or the Workplace Relations Act 1996.
@ref s 12A (src:372-372)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the instrument that gives the meaning of the expression` MEANS
    BRANCH IF elem expression (LIST "AWA", "collective agreement", "ITEA", "notional agreement preserving State awards", "old IR agreement", "pre-reform AWA", "pre-reform certified agreement", "preserved State agreement", "Division 2B State instrument", "State reference transitional award or common rule")
             THEN JUST "Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009"
           IF expression EQUALS "enterprise agreement" THEN JUST "Fair Work Act 2009"
           IF expression EQUALS "workplace determination" THEN JUST "Fair Work Act 2009 or Workplace Relations Act 1996"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
